   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Verbos + -ing",
   "texto": [
    "**enjoy** (disfrutar), **avoid** (evitar), **finish** (terminar), **suggest** (sugerir), **practise** (practicar), **consider** (considerar), **risk** (arriesgarse): **I enjoy swimming**, **She avoided answering**.",
    "Tras preposiciones siempre va -ing: **good at swimming**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Verbos + to",
   "texto": [
    "**want**, **hope**, **decide**, **plan**, **agree**, **refuse**, **manage**: **I hope to win**, **She refused to help**, **We manage to finish**.",
    "Estos verbos no admiten -ing después: no se dice «I hope winning»."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Los que admiten los dos",
   "texto": [
    "**Like**, **love**, **hate**, **prefer**, **start**: **I like swimming** = **I like to swim** (casi igual). Con **prefer** se usa sobre todo **prefer -ing**: **I prefer walking**."
   ]
